## Managed by Ansible (grafana_stack role) — do not edit by hand.
## Grafana unified-alerting file provisioning: alert rules.
## https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/latest/alerting/set-up/provision-alerting-resources/file-provisioning/
##
## Every rule below queries the "prometheus" datasource (infra metrics —
## grafana_stack/templates/datasource.yml.j2), which is provisioned only when
## a prometheus-tagged container exists (grafana_stack_prometheus_url). This
## whole file renders with zero groups otherwise, exactly like the community
## dashboards this role also skips when there is nothing for them to query.
##
## READY NOW vs DORMANT (see role README / PR evidence for detail):
##   - blackbox-probe-down   READY  — blackbox_exporter's probe_success is
##                                    scraped today (prometheus_stack role).
##   - infra-targets-down    READY  — `up` exists for every job prometheus.yml
##                                    actually renders today: prometheus,
##                                    blackbox_<module>, traefik, llm_router,
##                                    hindsight, agentgateway. There is NO
##                                    node/PVE scrape job yet — a per-PVE-node
##                                    up/down rule is not written here rather
##                                    than invented against a job label that
##                                    does not exist.
##   - hindsight-replica-count-low READY — up{job="hindsight"} is scraped
##                                    today (prometheus_stack role); counts
##                                    live replicas against the expected
##                                    total (grafana_stack_alert_hindsight_
##                                    min_replicas). Retain-failure-rate,
##                                    stuck-operations and memory_defense-
##                                    triggered alerts are NOT written here:
##                                    Hindsight's exported metrics
##                                    (hindsight_operation_operations_total,
##                                    scoped by operation/tenant/bank_id) carry
##                                    no success/failure or staleness label to
##                                    alert on yet — add them the moment
##                                    upstream exposes one, per the same
##                                    "no rule on a nonexistent metric" rule
##                                    every other DORMANT entry here follows.
##   - wan-latency-high      READY  — probe_duration_seconds{job="blackbox_icmp"}
##                                    is scraped today.
##   - disk-usage-high       READY  — node_filesystem_avail_bytes /
##                                    node_filesystem_size_bytes are scraped
##                                    today under job="pve_node_exporter"
##                                    (inventory/group_vars/prometheus_group.yml).
##   - secret-rotation-overdue DORMANT — depends on a node_exporter textfile
##                                     collector metric from the secret-age
##                                     auditor, a package not yet in develop.
##                                     Same noDataState: OK reasoning.
##
## AI-TELEMETRY ABSENCE RULES query the "victoriametrics" datasource instead
## (grafana_stack/templates/datasource.yml.j2). Unlike "prometheus" above,
## that datasource is provisioned unconditionally by this role — it is the
## role's own AI-observability backend, not gated behind any variable — so
## those rule groups sit outside the conditional block below and always
## render, independent of grafana_stack_prometheus_url.
##
## The absence-window split (15m vs 6h) is deliberate, not a tidy number:
##   - claude_code_token_usage_tokens_total / claude_code_cost_usage_USD_total
##     are pushed by a running process, so quiet is abnormal within minutes.
##   - claude_jsonl_cache_read_tokens_total / claude_jsonl_cache_creation_tokens_total
##     / codex_conversation_turn_count_total are launchd StartInterval timers
##     on a laptop. launchd timers do not fire while the machine sleeps, so a
##     15m window would page every night, get muted, and restore the exact
##     silence these rules exist to end.
##
## claude-jsonl-etl-frozen exists because a FROZEN writer passes every
## absence rule above: a cumulative counter that stops advancing while its
## series still exists is invisible to absent_over_time. Measured
## 2026-09-19: the JSONL cache-read sum sat at exactly 360.005B for 19
## consecutive 10-minute steps with no absence rule noticing.
##
## litellm_*, opencode_*, gen_ai* and vm_* are deliberately NOT covered here
## — none of them has any series in the store yet, and a rule on a
## nonexistent metric fires on load, gets muted, and restores the silence
## these rules exist to end. Add a rule the moment each source's first
## sample lands.
apiVersion: 1

groups:
{% if grafana_stack_prometheus_url | trim | length > 0 %}
  - orgId: 1
    name: {{ grafana_stack_alert_folder }}
    folder: {{ grafana_stack_alert_folder }}
    interval: {{ grafana_stack_alert_eval_interval }}
    rules:
      - uid: blackbox-probe-down
        title: Blackbox probe failing
        condition: B
        data:
          - refId: A
            relativeTimeRange: {from: 300, to: 0}
            datasourceUid: prometheus
            model:
              expr: probe_success == 0
              instant: true
              refId: A
          - refId: B
            relativeTimeRange: {from: 0, to: 0}
            datasourceUid: __expr__
            model:
              type: threshold
              expression: A
              conditions:
                - evaluator: {type: gt, params: [0]}
              refId: B
        for: 5m
        noDataState: OK
        execErrState: Alerting
        labels: {severity: critical}
        annotations:
          summary: "Blackbox probe {{ '{{' }} $labels.instance {{ '}}' }} ({{ '{{' }} $labels.job {{ '}}' }}) has failed for 5m."

      - uid: infra-targets-down
        title: Infra scrape target down
        condition: B
        data:
          - refId: A
            relativeTimeRange: {from: 300, to: 0}
            datasourceUid: prometheus
            model:
              expr: up{job=~"prometheus|blackbox_.*|traefik|llm_router|hindsight|agentgateway"} == 0
              instant: true
              refId: A
          - refId: B
            relativeTimeRange: {from: 0, to: 0}
            datasourceUid: __expr__
            model:
              type: threshold
              expression: A
              conditions:
                - evaluator: {type: gt, params: [0]}
              refId: B
        for: 5m
        noDataState: OK
        execErrState: Alerting
        labels: {severity: critical}
        annotations:
          summary: "Scrape target {{ '{{' }} $labels.instance {{ '}}' }} (job {{ '{{' }} $labels.job {{ '}}' }}) is down."

      - uid: hindsight-replica-count-low
        title: Hindsight replica count low
        condition: B
        data:
          - refId: A
            relativeTimeRange: {from: 300, to: 0}
            datasourceUid: prometheus
            model:
              expr: count(up{job="hindsight"} == 1)
              instant: true
              refId: A
          - refId: B
            relativeTimeRange: {from: 0, to: 0}
            datasourceUid: __expr__
            model:
              type: threshold
              expression: A
              conditions:
                - evaluator: {type: lt, params: [{{ grafana_stack_alert_hindsight_min_replicas }}]}
              refId: B
        for: 5m
        noDataState: Alerting
        execErrState: Alerting
        labels: {severity: critical}
        annotations:
          summary: >-
            Only {{ '{{' }} $values.A {{ '}}' }} Hindsight replica(s) up, below
            the expected {{ grafana_stack_alert_hindsight_min_replicas }}.

      - uid: wan-latency-high
        title: WAN ICMP latency high
        condition: B
        data:
          - refId: A
            relativeTimeRange: {from: 300, to: 0}
            datasourceUid: prometheus
            model:
              expr: avg_over_time(probe_duration_seconds{job="blackbox_icmp"}[5m])
              instant: true
              refId: A
          - refId: B
            relativeTimeRange: {from: 0, to: 0}
            datasourceUid: __expr__
            model:
              type: threshold
              expression: A
              conditions:
                - evaluator: {type: gt, params: [{{ grafana_stack_alert_wan_latency_seconds }}]}
              refId: B
        for: 10m
        noDataState: OK
        execErrState: Alerting
        labels: {severity: warning}
        annotations:
          summary: "WAN ICMP latency to {{ '{{' }} $labels.instance {{ '}}' }} averaged above {{ grafana_stack_alert_wan_latency_seconds }}s over 5m."

      - uid: disk-usage-high
        title: Disk usage high
        condition: B
        data:
          - refId: A
            relativeTimeRange: {from: 300, to: 0}
            datasourceUid: prometheus
            model:
              expr: >-
                100 * (1 - node_filesystem_avail_bytes{job="pve_node_exporter", fstype!~"tmpfs|overlay"}
                / node_filesystem_size_bytes{job="pve_node_exporter", fstype!~"tmpfs|overlay"})
              instant: true
              refId: A
          - refId: B
            relativeTimeRange: {from: 0, to: 0}
            datasourceUid: __expr__
            model:
              type: threshold
              expression: A
              conditions:
                - evaluator: {type: gt, params: [{{ grafana_stack_alert_disk_pct }}]}
              refId: B
        for: 15m
        noDataState: OK
        execErrState: Alerting
        labels: {severity: warning}
        annotations:
          summary: "Disk usage on {{ '{{' }} $labels.instance {{ '}}' }} ({{ '{{' }} $labels.mountpoint {{ '}}' }}) above {{ grafana_stack_alert_disk_pct }}%."

      # DORMANT — see file header. secret_age_days is a future textfile-collector
      # metric from a separate secret-age-audit package, not present in develop.
      - uid: secret-rotation-overdue
        title: Secret rotation overdue (dormant until secret-age exporter lands)
        condition: B
        data:
          - refId: A
            relativeTimeRange: {from: 300, to: 0}
            datasourceUid: prometheus
            model:
              expr: secret_age_days
              instant: true
              refId: A
          - refId: B
            relativeTimeRange: {from: 0, to: 0}
            datasourceUid: __expr__
            model:
              type: threshold
              expression: A
              conditions:
                - evaluator: {type: gte, params: [{{ grafana_stack_alert_secret_age_days }}]}
              refId: B
        for: 0m
        noDataState: OK
        execErrState: OK
        labels: {severity: warning}
        annotations:
          summary: "Secret {{ '{{' }} $labels.path {{ '}}' }} is {{ '{{' }} $values.A {{ '}}' }} days old (>= {{ grafana_stack_alert_secret_age_days }})."
{% endif %}
  # AI telemetry absence checks — see file header for the interval-split and
  # frozen-writer rationale. Datasource is "victoriametrics", provisioned
  # unconditionally, so this group (and the two below) always render.
  - orgId: 1
    name: ai-telemetry-absence-pushed
    folder: {{ grafana_stack_alert_folder }}
    interval: {{ grafana_stack_alert_eval_interval }}
    rules:
      - uid: claude-code-telemetry-absent
        title: Claude Code token telemetry absent
        condition: B
        data:
          - refId: A
            relativeTimeRange: {from: 300, to: 0}
            datasourceUid: victoriametrics
            model:
              expr: absent_over_time(claude_code_token_usage_tokens_total[15m])
              instant: true
              refId: A
          - refId: B
            relativeTimeRange: {from: 0, to: 0}
            datasourceUid: __expr__
            model:
              type: threshold
              expression: A
              conditions:
                - evaluator: {type: gt, params: [0]}
              refId: B
        for: 15m
        noDataState: OK
        execErrState: Alerting
        labels: {severity: warning, stream: claude-code}
        annotations:
          summary: "Claude Code has emitted no token telemetry for 15 minutes."

      - uid: claude-code-cost-absent
        title: Claude Code cost telemetry absent
        condition: B
        data:
          - refId: A
            relativeTimeRange: {from: 300, to: 0}
            datasourceUid: victoriametrics
            model:
              expr: absent_over_time(claude_code_cost_usage_USD_total[15m])
              instant: true
              refId: A
          - refId: B
            relativeTimeRange: {from: 0, to: 0}
            datasourceUid: __expr__
            model:
              type: threshold
              expression: A
              conditions:
                - evaluator: {type: gt, params: [0]}
              refId: B
        for: 15m
        noDataState: OK
        execErrState: Alerting
        labels: {severity: warning, stream: claude-code}
        annotations:
          summary: "Claude Code has emitted no cost telemetry for 15 minutes."

  # Timer-driven streams on a machine that legitimately sleeps — see file
  # header. 6h tolerates an overnight sleep without paging, while still
  # catching a collector that has genuinely stopped. Tighten only for a
  # source on an always-on host.
  - orgId: 1
    name: ai-telemetry-absence-timered
    folder: {{ grafana_stack_alert_folder }}
    interval: 5m
    rules:
      - uid: claude-jsonl-etl-absent
        title: Claude JSONL ETL telemetry absent
        condition: B
        data:
          - refId: A
            relativeTimeRange: {from: 300, to: 0}
            datasourceUid: victoriametrics
            model:
              expr: absent_over_time(claude_jsonl_cache_read_tokens_total[6h])
              instant: true
              refId: A
          - refId: B
            relativeTimeRange: {from: 0, to: 0}
            datasourceUid: __expr__
            model:
              type: threshold
              expression: A
              conditions:
                - evaluator: {type: gt, params: [0]}
              refId: B
        for: 30m
        noDataState: OK
        execErrState: Alerting
        labels: {severity: warning, stream: claude-jsonl-etl}
        annotations:
          summary: >-
            Claude JSONL ETL has pushed nothing for 6 hours. Check whether
            the machine slept before suspecting the collector — launchd
            timers do not fire while asleep.

      - uid: claude-jsonl-cache-tier-absent
        title: Claude JSONL cache-tier telemetry absent
        condition: B
        data:
          - refId: A
            relativeTimeRange: {from: 300, to: 0}
            datasourceUid: victoriametrics
            model:
              expr: absent_over_time(claude_jsonl_cache_creation_tokens_total[6h])
              instant: true
              refId: A
          - refId: B
            relativeTimeRange: {from: 0, to: 0}
            datasourceUid: __expr__
            model:
              type: threshold
              expression: A
              conditions:
                - evaluator: {type: gt, params: [0]}
              refId: B
        for: 30m
        noDataState: OK
        execErrState: Alerting
        labels: {severity: warning, stream: claude-jsonl-etl}
        annotations:
          summary: >-
            No Claude JSONL cache-creation telemetry for 6 hours; the 5m/1h
            cache-tier split is blind until this recovers.

      - uid: codex-telemetry-absent
        title: Codex telemetry absent
        condition: B
        data:
          - refId: A
            relativeTimeRange: {from: 300, to: 0}
            datasourceUid: victoriametrics
            model:
              expr: absent_over_time(codex_conversation_turn_count_total[6h])
              instant: true
              refId: A
          - refId: B
            relativeTimeRange: {from: 0, to: 0}
            datasourceUid: __expr__
            model:
              type: threshold
              expression: A
              conditions:
                - evaluator: {type: gt, params: [0]}
              refId: B
        for: 30m
        noDataState: OK
        execErrState: Alerting
        labels: {severity: warning, stream: codex}
        annotations:
          summary: "Codex has emitted no turn telemetry for 6 hours."

  # A frozen writer is NOT an absent one — see file header. A cumulative
  # counter that stops advancing while its series still exists passes every
  # absence rule above.
  - orgId: 1
    name: ai-telemetry-staleness
    folder: {{ grafana_stack_alert_folder }}
    interval: 5m
    rules:
      - uid: claude-jsonl-etl-frozen
        title: Claude JSONL ETL frozen (series present, not advancing)
        condition: B
        data:
          - refId: A
            relativeTimeRange: {from: 300, to: 0}
            datasourceUid: victoriametrics
            model:
              expr: increase(claude_jsonl_cache_read_tokens_total[6h])
              instant: true
              refId: A
          - refId: B
            relativeTimeRange: {from: 0, to: 0}
            datasourceUid: __expr__
            model:
              type: threshold
              expression: A
              conditions:
                - evaluator: {type: lte, params: [0]}
              refId: B
        for: 1h
        noDataState: OK
        execErrState: Alerting
        labels: {severity: warning, stream: claude-jsonl-etl}
        annotations:
          summary: "Claude JSONL ETL series exist but have not advanced in 6 hours."
